      "heading_context": "## The Critical Zone Concept",
      "confidence": "candidate",
      "text": "CRITICAL ZONE ARCHITECTURE:\n\n  ABOVE GROUND BIOMASS\n  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  LITTER / ORGANIC HORIZON (O)  : 0–5 cm\n  TOPSOIL (A horizon)           : 0–30 cm      <-- most biologically active\n  SUBSOIL (B horizon)           : 30–100 cm    <-- accumulation zone\n  WEATHERED PARENT MATERIAL (C) : 0.5–5 m      <-- active weathering front\n  SAPROLITE (partially weathered): up to 10–30 m\n  FRESH BEDROCK (R)             :              <-- ultimate mineral source\n  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  GROUNDWATER ZONE               : depth variable\n\n  KEY RATES:\n  Soil formation: ~0.01–0.1 mm/yr (most soils) to ~1 mm/yr (young volcanic)\n  Soil erosion (unprotected cultivated): ~1–10 mm/yr\n  --> Most agricultural soils are losing soil faster than it forms\n  Biological activity: concentrated in top 15–30 cm",
