      "confidence": "candidate",
      "text": "High CEC means high capacity to hold cation nutrients (Ca2+, Mg2+, K+, NH4+); it does not mean those nutrients are present. A high-CEC soil can be nutrient-deficient. CEC is a structural property; nutrient content requires separate measurement.",
